        t["SHIFTER"]["shift"] = LearnEntry{"Moves the WHOLE spectrum by so many HERTZ (−2000..2000, +CV on SFT: 1 unit = 1000 Hz). 0 = straight through. Because the shift is in Hz and not a ratio, the partials stop being harmonic → metallic, bell-like.", "Frequency shifter (SSB — single sideband): unlike SHAPE's ring-mod, which gives BOTH sidebands (sum and difference) symmetrically. Here `up` = spectrum + shift, `down` = spectrum − shift, each on its own output.", "A small Δf (5–20 Hz) = a 'phaser' that never closes (the two copies beat slowly). A large Δf = inharmonic clangour."};
        t["SHIFTER"]["feedback"] = LearnEntry{"Part of the `up` output goes back into the input → the spectrum rises again, and again: an infinite glissando (Shepard's 'barber pole' / shimmer). A negative `feedback` pulls from `down` (it falls without stopping). `tanh` in the loop — it never blows up.", "", "SHIFT ~8 Hz + FEEDBACK ~0.8 = Risset's rope, rising eternally."};
